{
  "about": [
    "The functions a statement typed in the SQL tab may call, per engine. Everything else is refused.",
    "A function is refused unless it is listed here: under 'all' (every engine) or under its engine.",
    "Why a list of what is allowed: a function can do anything - sleep, take a lock, read a file, call",
    "another server, or write through an autonomous transaction (a user-defined function in Oracle).",
    "A list of known-bad names would always be one name short.",
    "Only add built-in functions that read their arguments and return a value. Never add a function",
    "your own database defines unless you have read its code.",
    "Edit this file and restart the app. For one PC only, the environment variable",
    "DATA_EXPLORER_SQL_FUNCTIONS=my_func,oracle:other_func adds names without touching the file.",
    "'types' are type names that may be followed by a bracket: VARCHAR(10), NUMBER(10, 2)."
